{
  "$comment": [
    "Central model registry for the massa-ai agent harness. THE only hand-authored place",
    "that names a model or an effort level for any host.",
    "",
    "V2 SHAPE: `models` is a dropdown catalog only (D4) -- a profile CELL stores the",
    "resolved model string directly, never a catalog id, so a cell can never dangle.",
    "`profiles.<name>.hosts.<host>` is that profile's default cell for a tool;",
    "`profiles.<name>.agents.<agent>.<host>` is an optional per-agent override, resolved",
    "before the host default (see `resolveAgent` in scripts/lib/model-profiles.ts).",
    "",
    "PROFILE SELECTION: --profile=<name> > MASSA_AI_MODEL_PROFILE > install-state's recorded",
    "profile > \"balanced\". An unknown profile, or a (profile, host) pair the profile does",
    "not support, is a hard error. Nothing silently falls back to a default model.",
    "",
    "model: null means 'do not pin -- inherit'. Every host documents that semantic, but",
    "spells it differently, so the emitters render it per host.",
    "",
    "Adding a profile is data-only: no TypeScript type, enum, or test enumerates these names.",
    "See .specs/features/model-catalog-revamp/spec.md."
  ],
  "version": 2,

  "models": {
